1
00:00:01,418 --> 00:00:04,045
Hey, you guys,
I got some bad news.
What?

2
00:00:04,087 --> 00:00:06,256
Well, that's no way
to sell newspapers.

3
00:00:06,298 --> 00:00:09,551
Try, "Extra, extra,
read all about it!"

4
00:00:09,593 --> 00:00:13,973
No, Monica's restaurant got
a horrible review in the Post.

5
00:00:14,014 --> 00:00:15,766
Oh, no!
Oh, no!

6
00:00:15,808 --> 00:00:17,518
Yeah, I didn't want
her to see it,
so I ran around

7
00:00:17,559 --> 00:00:20,604
the neighborhood and bought
all the copies I could find.

8
00:00:20,646 --> 00:00:22,272
Man, this is bad.

9
00:00:22,314 --> 00:00:24,566
And I've had my share
of bad reviews.

10
00:00:24,608 --> 00:00:26,360
I still remember
my first good one, though.

11
00:00:26,401 --> 00:00:28,696
"Everything else in this
production of Our Town

12
00:00:28,737 --> 00:00:29,780
"was simply terrible.

13
00:00:29,822 --> 00:00:33,158
Joey Tribbiani was abysmal."

14
00:00:35,828 --> 00:00:37,621
Hey... Oh, my God.

15
00:00:37,663 --> 00:00:39,498
Look at all
the newspapers.

16
00:00:39,540 --> 00:00:40,958
It must be a good review.

17
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:42,083
Is it great?

18
00:00:42,125 --> 00:00:43,752
Um...

19
00:00:47,464 --> 00:00:48,966
Oh, dear God.

20
00:00:49,008 --> 00:00:50,467
But the good news is

21
00:00:50,509 --> 00:00:53,178
no one in a two-block radius
will ever know.

22
00:00:54,053 --> 00:00:56,223
What about the rest
of Manhattan?

23
00:00:56,264 --> 00:00:58,308
Yeah, they all know.

24
00:00:58,350 --> 00:01:00,811
Oh, my God,
this is horrible.

25
00:01:00,853 --> 00:01:03,022
I'm so sorry, honey.
I'm so humiliated.

26
00:01:03,104 --> 00:01:04,940
Yeah, but you know
what they say, Mon:

27
00:01:04,982 --> 00:01:06,775
there is no such thing
as bad press.

28
00:01:06,817 --> 00:01:08,610
You don't think
that, um

29
00:01:08,652 --> 00:01:12,447
"The chef's mahi-mahi
was awful awful"
is bad press?

30
00:01:14,033 --> 00:01:16,368
I didn't write it.

31
00:01:16,410 --> 00:01:17,703
Oh, my God, is he right?

32
00:01:17,745 --> 00:01:19,120
Am I really... am I awful?

33
00:01:19,162 --> 00:01:20,455
ALL:
No.

34
00:01:20,497 --> 00:01:22,041
Hey, Monica,
you listen to me, okay?

35
00:01:22,082 --> 00:01:23,959
And I'm not just saying this
'cause I'm your friend.

36
00:01:24,001 --> 00:01:26,587
I'm saying it
'cause it's the truth.

37
00:01:26,628 --> 00:01:28,255
Your food is abysmal.

38
00:01:35,387 --> 00:01:40,642
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪

39
00:01:40,684 --> 00:01:42,895
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

40
00:01:42,937 --> 00:01:45,022
♪ Your love life's D.O.A. ♪

41
00:01:45,064 --> 00:01:49,860
♪ It's like you're always
stuck in second gear ♪

42
00:01:49,902 --> 00:01:52,153
♪ When it hasn't been
your day, your week ♪

43
00:01:52,195 --> 00:01:55,407
♪ Your month,
or even your year ♪

44
00:01:55,449 --> 00:01:58,702
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

45
00:01:58,744 --> 00:02:04,750
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

46
00:02:13,132 --> 00:02:13,759
Ross?!

47
00:02:13,801 --> 00:02:16,303
What? What?

48
00:02:16,344 --> 00:02:18,013
I am freaking out.

49
00:02:18,055 --> 00:02:19,890
Are you?

50
00:02:19,932 --> 00:02:22,601
My due date is in one week.

51
00:02:22,643 --> 00:02:23,602
What are you doing up?

52
00:02:23,644 --> 00:02:25,729
That is seven days.

53
00:02:25,771 --> 00:02:27,982
Okay, look, I had a lot of water
before I went to bed.

54
00:02:28,023 --> 00:02:29,066
Can we do this after...?

55
00:02:29,108 --> 00:02:30,609
No, no, no, no, no, Ross.

56
00:02:30,651 --> 00:02:32,111
Please, come on--

57
00:02:32,152 --> 00:02:33,904
we do not have any
of the big stuff that we need.

58
00:02:33,946 --> 00:02:35,906
We do not have
a changing table.

59
00:02:35,948 --> 00:02:37,449
We do not have
a crib.

60
00:02:37,491 --> 00:02:39,159
We do not have a diaper service.

61
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:41,662
It's funny you should
mention diapers.

62
00:02:42,788 --> 00:02:44,081
I'm serious.

63
00:02:44,123 --> 00:02:45,666
Okay, look, there's nothing
to worry about.

64
00:02:45,707 --> 00:02:47,208
We have plenty of time.

65
00:02:47,250 --> 00:02:49,544
There's a great
baby furniture store
on West Tenth.

66
00:02:49,586 --> 00:02:51,505
Tomorrow we will
go there

67
00:02:51,546 --> 00:02:53,256
and we'll get you
everything we need, okay?

68
00:02:53,298 --> 00:02:54,591
Okay. Thank you.

69
00:02:54,633 --> 00:02:55,843
That's great.
Thank you.

70
00:02:55,884 --> 00:02:57,803
Wait, wait, where
on West Tenth?

71
00:02:57,845 --> 00:02:59,387
'Cause there's a really
cute shoe store
that has, like...

72
00:02:59,429 --> 00:03:02,016
Okay, okay, if, uh,
if you're going to do this

73
00:03:02,057 --> 00:03:04,018
then I'm going
to go do that, so...

74
00:03:04,059 --> 00:03:05,644
Oh, wait, Ross,
I'm sorry.

75
00:03:05,686 --> 00:03:06,812
One more thing.

76
00:03:06,854 --> 00:03:07,855
Yeah?!

77
00:03:07,896 --> 00:03:09,898
Um, our situation, you know?

78
00:03:09,940 --> 00:03:12,151
Um, what we mean to each other?

79
00:03:12,191 --> 00:03:13,443
And, I mean

80
00:03:13,485 --> 00:03:15,236
we're having this
baby together, you know

81
00:03:15,278 --> 00:03:16,864
and we live together.

82
00:03:16,905 --> 00:03:17,865
( sighing )

83
00:03:17,906 --> 00:03:20,575
Isn't that... isn't that weird?

84
00:03:26,205 --> 00:03:28,125
Well, uh...

85
00:03:28,167 --> 00:03:30,127
I'm just kidding;
you can go pee.

86
00:03:34,882 --> 00:03:36,508
Hey, uh, Monica,
I can't remember.

87
00:03:36,550 --> 00:03:39,178
Did we say we were
going to meet here
or at the movie?

88
00:03:39,219 --> 00:03:40,137
At the movies, but...

89
00:03:40,179 --> 00:03:41,221
Okay, I'll see you there.

90
00:03:41,262 --> 00:03:44,016
Joey...
now that you're here...

91
00:03:44,058 --> 00:03:46,434
Sure, I can hang out
till I have to meet you.

92
00:03:47,686 --> 00:03:49,354
But how come
you're not going?

93
00:03:49,396 --> 00:03:50,731
I can't.
I've got a job interview

94
00:03:50,772 --> 00:03:52,024
I got to get ready for.

95
00:03:52,066 --> 00:03:53,650
I thought you already
have a job.

96
00:03:53,692 --> 00:03:55,903
And people say
you don't pay attention.

97
00:03:57,278 --> 00:03:58,822
No, no, this is
a much better job.

98
00:03:58,864 --> 00:04:00,323
It's vice-president
of the company

99
00:04:00,365 --> 00:04:01,867
that does data reconfiguration

100
00:04:01,909 --> 00:04:03,869
and statistical factoring
for other companies.

101
00:04:06,163 --> 00:04:08,707
Wow. How do you know
how to do that?

102
00:04:08,749 --> 00:04:11,418
That's what I do now.

103
00:04:11,459 --> 00:04:13,461
Hey, Joey,
come taste this.

104
00:04:13,503 --> 00:04:14,922
What is it?

105
00:04:14,963 --> 00:04:16,631
Remember that guy
that gave me a bad review?

106
00:04:16,673 --> 00:04:18,550
Well...

107
00:04:18,592 --> 00:04:20,135
I'm getting my revenge.

108
00:04:21,970 --> 00:04:24,181
You cooked him?

109
00:04:24,223 --> 00:04:28,227
No. He teaches a course
on food criticism
at the New School.

110
00:04:28,268 --> 00:04:30,187
Before we go to the movies,
I'm going to go there

111
00:04:30,229 --> 00:04:32,064
and make him try
my bouillabaisse again.

112
00:04:32,106 --> 00:04:34,608
Oh, I can't wait
to read the front page
of the Post tomorrow.

113
00:04:34,649 --> 00:04:36,735
"Restaurant reviewer
admits

114
00:04:36,777 --> 00:04:39,071
'I was wrong
about Monica.'"

115
00:04:40,197 --> 00:04:41,448
The front page?

116
00:04:41,489 --> 00:04:43,158
MONICA:
Mm-hmm.

117
00:04:43,200 --> 00:04:45,368
You really do live in your
own little world, don't you?

118
00:04:51,332 --> 00:04:54,169
Do you, uh, want
these things delivered,
Mr. and Mrs. Geller?

119
00:04:54,211 --> 00:04:55,378
Oh, no, no, no.

120
00:04:55,420 --> 00:04:57,756
No, no, no,
we're not married.

121
00:04:57,798 --> 00:05:00,675
We are having a baby together,
but we're not involved.

122
00:05:02,052 --> 00:05:06,723
I mean, uh, we, we, we were
seeing each other a while ago

123
00:05:06,765 --> 00:05:08,433
but then we were just friends

124
00:05:08,475 --> 00:05:10,644
and then there
was one drunken night...

125
00:05:13,396 --> 00:05:16,566
Or, "Yes, stranger, we'd like
this delivered, please."

126
00:05:16,608 --> 00:05:19,444
Why don't you fill out
this address card?

127
00:05:19,486 --> 00:05:21,320
Oh, okay.

128
00:05:21,362 --> 00:05:22,948
I noticed you've
picked out a lot
of our dinosaur items.

129
00:05:22,990 --> 00:05:24,699
RACHEL:
Oh, yeah.

130
00:05:24,741 --> 00:05:27,202
Actually, that's one of the
reasons why we are not a couple.

131
00:05:28,703 --> 00:05:29,704
I chose those.

132
00:05:29,746 --> 00:05:30,998
I'm a paleontologist.

133
00:05:31,039 --> 00:05:31,999
Really?

134
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:33,750
That is so cool.

135
00:05:33,792 --> 00:05:36,086
Oh, oh, yeah, don't get
too worked up over it.

136
00:05:36,128 --> 00:05:38,672
I mean, it sounds like
he's a doctor, but he's not.

137
00:05:38,713 --> 00:05:40,381
Oh, no, no.

138
00:05:40,423 --> 00:05:41,967
I'm fascinated
by paleontology.

139
00:05:42,009 --> 00:05:44,136
Have you read the new
Walter Alvarez book?

140
00:05:44,178 --> 00:05:46,554
I teach it in my class.

141
00:05:46,596 --> 00:05:47,764
Oh, my God.

142
00:05:47,806 --> 00:05:49,183
I'm standing
at a cash register

143
00:05:49,224 --> 00:05:52,644
I'm holding a credit card,
and I'm bored.

144
00:05:52,686 --> 00:05:54,729
Oh, I love
your neighborhood.

145
00:05:54,771 --> 00:05:57,107
There's a great gym
right around the corner
from your building.

146
00:05:57,149 --> 00:05:58,233
That's my gym.

147
00:05:58,275 --> 00:06:00,152
I could tell you work out.

148
00:06:05,573 --> 00:06:08,327
A paleontologist
who works out.

149
00:06:08,367 --> 00:06:10,871
You're like Indiana Jones.

150
00:06:14,333 --> 00:06:17,002
I am like Indiana Jones.

151
00:06:23,217 --> 00:06:24,843
Hi, Pheebs.

152
00:06:24,885 --> 00:06:27,762
Hey. Oh, how did
baby shopping go?

153
00:06:27,804 --> 00:06:28,972
Oh, it was great.

154
00:06:29,014 --> 00:06:30,389
We got everything
that we needed.

155
00:06:30,431 --> 00:06:32,351
Oh, and Ross almost
got something

156
00:06:32,391 --> 00:06:33,852
that wasn't on the list.

157
00:06:33,894 --> 00:06:34,853
( clearing throat )

158
00:06:34,895 --> 00:06:35,896
A whore.

159
00:06:37,522 --> 00:06:38,690
What?

160
00:06:38,732 --> 00:06:41,026
Well, we were paying
for our stuff

161
00:06:41,068 --> 00:06:44,321
and this saleswoman just
started flirting with him.

162
00:06:44,363 --> 00:06:45,780
Can you believe that?

163
00:06:45,822 --> 00:06:47,615
Well, did she know
you two weren't married?

164
00:06:47,657 --> 00:06:49,076
Yeah.

165
00:06:50,244 --> 00:06:51,619
Oh, my God.

166
00:06:53,121 --> 00:06:56,124
Well, the idea--
a woman flirting
with a single man--

167
00:06:56,166 --> 00:06:58,710
we must alert
the church elders.

168
00:06:58,752 --> 00:07:00,670
No, you don't understand.

169
00:07:00,712 --> 00:07:03,340
You didn't see
how brazen she was.

170
00:07:03,382 --> 00:07:05,342
It sounds like you're
a little jealous.

171
00:07:05,384 --> 00:07:06,634
No, I'm not.

172
00:07:06,676 --> 00:07:09,388
I-I-I just think it's wrong.

173
00:07:09,428 --> 00:07:11,390
It, I mean, here I am
about to pop

174
00:07:11,431 --> 00:07:13,641
and he's out picking up
some shop girl

175
00:07:13,683 --> 00:07:15,727
at Sluts 'R Us?

176
00:07:15,769 --> 00:07:18,272
Is that a real place?

177
00:07:19,438 --> 00:07:21,066
Are they hiring?

178
00:07:22,776 --> 00:07:25,028
Hey, Phoebe. Fatty.

179
00:07:27,114 --> 00:07:29,324
Hey, Chandler,
why so fancy?

180
00:07:29,366 --> 00:07:30,409
Well, I got
a job interview.

181
00:07:30,450 --> 00:07:31,534
It's kind of
a big deal, too.

182
00:07:31,576 --> 00:07:32,869
It's a lot more money

183
00:07:32,911 --> 00:07:34,162
and I'd be doing
data reconfiguration

184
00:07:34,204 --> 00:07:35,622
and statistical factoring.

185
00:07:35,663 --> 00:07:37,332
Wait, I think I know
someone who does that.

186
00:07:37,374 --> 00:07:39,293
Me. I do that.

187
00:07:40,794 --> 00:07:42,379
So, seriously, do I,
do I look okay?

188
00:07:42,421 --> 00:07:43,671
I'm a little nervous.

189
00:07:43,713 --> 00:07:45,590
Oh, yeah, you really,
you look great.

190
00:07:45,632 --> 00:07:47,634
Just don't get your hopes up.

191
00:07:49,469 --> 00:07:50,429
Why not?

192
00:07:50,469 --> 00:07:52,055
Well, the interview.

193
00:07:52,097 --> 00:07:53,765
What about it?

194
00:07:53,807 --> 00:07:55,642
You know. You don't make
a very good first impression.

195
00:07:57,311 --> 00:07:58,561
What?

196
00:07:58,603 --> 00:08:00,605
Oh, you don't know.

197
00:08:00,647 --> 00:08:02,399
Are you serious?

198
00:08:02,441 --> 00:08:03,984
Yes. When I first
met you

199
00:08:04,025 --> 00:08:05,568
you were, like...
( speaking gibberish )

200
00:08:05,610 --> 00:08:06,569
It was, like...

201
00:08:06,611 --> 00:08:08,989
Shh!

202
00:08:10,782 --> 00:08:13,493
What is it that I do?

203
00:08:13,534 --> 00:08:15,745
Well, it's just like
you're trying too hard--

204
00:08:15,787 --> 00:08:17,289
always making jokes, you know?

205
00:08:17,331 --> 00:08:18,706
You come off a little needy.

206
00:08:20,208 --> 00:08:22,585
Did you like me
when we first met?

207
00:08:22,627 --> 00:08:24,921
Chandler, I'm not going to lie
to you.

208
00:08:24,963 --> 00:08:27,590
But I am going to run away
from you.

209
00:08:31,970 --> 00:08:34,014
Hi.

210
00:08:34,055 --> 00:08:35,056
Um, I'm Monica Geller.

211
00:08:35,098 --> 00:08:36,183
I'm the chef at Alesandro's.

212
00:08:36,224 --> 00:08:37,434
Still?

213
00:08:37,476 --> 00:08:38,893
I think the things

214
00:08:38,935 --> 00:08:40,687
that you said
about me were really unfair

215
00:08:40,728 --> 00:08:41,980
and I would like
for you

216
00:08:42,022 --> 00:08:44,274
to give my bouillabaisse
another chance.

217
00:08:44,316 --> 00:08:45,608
I don't see
any reason

218
00:08:45,650 --> 00:08:47,361
why I would do that
to myself again.

219
00:08:47,402 --> 00:08:49,279
Either eat it
or be in it.

220
00:08:50,864 --> 00:08:52,366
Spoon?

221
00:08:52,407 --> 00:08:54,409
( clearing throat )

222
00:08:57,536 --> 00:08:58,830
So, what do you think?

223
00:08:58,872 --> 00:09:01,500
I'm torn...
between my integrity

224
00:09:01,540 --> 00:09:04,294
and my desire
to avoid a beating.

225
00:09:04,336 --> 00:09:06,629
But I must
be honest.

226
00:09:06,671 --> 00:09:09,466
Your soup...
is abysmal.

227
00:09:11,592 --> 00:09:13,594
Attagirl!

228
00:09:13,636 --> 00:09:15,305
Huh?!

229
00:09:15,347 --> 00:09:16,348
We should get out of here.

230
00:09:16,390 --> 00:09:17,516
There's a new class
coming in.

231
00:09:17,557 --> 00:09:19,059
Welcome to "Introduction
to Cooking."

232
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:20,227
Now, before we start

233
00:09:20,268 --> 00:09:21,936
can anyone tell me
the difference

234
00:09:21,978 --> 00:09:24,356
between a hollandaise
and a béarnaise sauce?

235
00:09:26,858 --> 00:09:27,859
I can.

236
00:09:27,901 --> 00:09:29,027
Okay. Go ahead.

237
00:09:29,069 --> 00:09:31,112
Well, they both have

238
00:09:31,154 --> 00:09:33,031
an egg yolk
and butter base

239
00:09:33,073 --> 00:09:36,201
but a béarnaise has
shallots, chervil

240
00:09:36,243 --> 00:09:37,869
and, most importantly,
tarragon.

241
00:09:37,911 --> 00:09:39,162
Oh, that's very good.

242
00:09:39,204 --> 00:09:40,205
What's your name?

243
00:09:40,247 --> 00:09:41,540
Monica.
Monica

244
00:09:41,581 --> 00:09:42,832
you go to the head
of the class.

245
00:09:42,874 --> 00:09:45,043
Okay.

246
00:09:47,003 --> 00:09:50,382
Wow, all this stuff
takes up a lot of room.

247
00:09:50,424 --> 00:09:52,050
Hey, how serious
are you

248
00:09:52,092 --> 00:09:54,177
about keeping Ben
in your life?

249
00:09:54,219 --> 00:09:55,678
My son?

250
00:09:55,720 --> 00:09:56,846
Pretty serious.

251
00:09:56,888 --> 00:09:58,932
( knock on door )

252
00:10:04,354 --> 00:10:05,355
Well, hey, Katie.

253
00:10:05,397 --> 00:10:06,981
What are you doing here?

254
00:10:07,023 --> 00:10:08,525
Well, the delivery went out
to you

255
00:10:08,567 --> 00:10:09,984
and I realized
they forgot this.

256
00:10:10,026 --> 00:10:11,736
Must have been fairly obvious

257
00:10:11,778 --> 00:10:14,531
since it was the only thing left
in your store.

258
00:10:14,573 --> 00:10:17,658
Listen...
to be honest

259
00:10:17,700 --> 00:10:21,788
home deliveries aren't
really part of my
job description.

260
00:10:21,829 --> 00:10:23,790
Oh.

261
00:10:23,831 --> 00:10:25,833
